WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.617
In Power, nobody presses anything.

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:10.512
When an agent in the campaign is available, the dialer reserves that agent,

00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:12.325
then calls the customer.

00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:16.917
Each call has its own reserved agent, so it never rings more customers

00:00:16.917 --> 00:00:18.730
than it has free agents.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:25.426
While it rings, the agent is Reserved, and the screen says waiting for a connected call.

00:00:25.426 --> 00:00:30.740
When a person answers, the agent is joined, and the activity opens on its own.

00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:34.620
Choose Power, and the form grows.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.705
Calls per agent is the most calls the dialer may start each time

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:41.622
it looks at the campaign, from one to three.

00:00:41.622 --> 00:00:44.365
Each of them reserves a free agent first.

00:00:44.907 --> 00:00:50.769
Power adds ring time, answering machine screening, and Show each dial to the agent.

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:53.667
It also adds the Abandoned calls card.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:58.072
What can go wrong is an abandoned call.

00:00:58.072 --> 00:01:03.122
A person answers, and no agent is connected within two seconds, for example

00:01:03.122 --> 00:01:05.802
because the agent's phone was closed.

00:01:05.802 --> 00:01:09.667
The person hears the abandoned call message, or silence.

00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:14.788
A voicemail, a busy line or no answer never reaches the agent.

00:01:14.788 --> 00:01:20.637
The dialer records the outcome itself, and the agent goes straight back to Available.

